<title>USA: Bond lwyrs urge technical changes to hedging rules.</title>
<headline>Bond lwyrs urge technical changes to hedging rules.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Bond Lawyers proposed what it calls minor revisions to amendments issued temporarily by the Internal Revenue Service in May 1994 to the Service' arbitrage rebate regulations.</p>
<p>The 1994 amendments deal with a variety of issues, including those conditions under which bonds with interest rate caps can be considered &quot;hedges&quot; against volatility instead of investment opportunities.</p>
<p>Lawyers are recommending revisions because the temporary regulations expire on May 10, 1997.</p>
<p>--Vicky Stamas, 202-898-8314</p>
</text>
